    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Increase metformin to 1000 mg twice daily and set an individualized HbA1c goal below 7.5%; avoid insulin and sulfonylureas while autonomic neuropathy may blunt warning symptoms of hypoglycemia. Guideline: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2025 (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes and glaucoma monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Treat neurogenic orthostatic hypotension: stand up in stages, raise the head of the bed, use waist-high compression, drink 2 liters of fluid a day, then midodrine with the last dose at least four hours before bed; check supine blood pressure at each visit. Guideline: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2025 (2025) [S]</item><item>Check HbA1c every three months until at goal, a basic metabolic panel, UACR, and lipids each year, lipids 4 to 12 weeks after starting a statin, and vitamin B12 periodically on metformin. Guideline: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2025 (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes and glaucoma monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Examine the feet at every visit because of sensory loss; daily self-inspection and protective footwear. Guideline: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2025 (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes and glaucoma monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Coordinate glaucoma care with the eye clinic: add dorzolamide to latanoprost, check pressure at each visit, and repeat OCT and visual fields every six months; avoid timolol and brimonidine because of bradycardia, bronchospasm, and low blood pressure. Guideline: Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Preferred Practice Pattern (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, diabetes and glaucoma monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Annual dilated eye examination for diabetic retinopathy; low-vision rehabilitation and home lighting review. Guideline: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2025 (2025); Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma Preferred Practice Pattern (2025) [S]</item><item>Start atorvastatin 40 mg; give PCV20 and recombinant zoster vaccines. Guideline: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2025 (2025) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
